    "notes": "The 24 consonants, in the order d t v f b p g k θ ð s z ʃ ʒ tʃ dʒ h ɹ j m n ŋ l w: each is said alone one to three times while only its symbol is on screen, then in three words; there is no review at the end. Every clip is the first time the sound is said alone. Another speaker than the vowel and diphthong videos of the same channel, which looks like a compilation of recordings from elsewhere — confirm that the uploader owns the recording before relying on the CC BY label. /θ/, /h/, /f/ and /p/ are only 5–15 dB above the noise floor of the recording and needed a large gain; /f/ has less padding after it because \"staff\" follows at once.",
